{
  "abstract": "Let $k \\geq 3$ and $G$ be a biplanar graph that is not $k$-colourable, of minimum order, with a fixed planar partition of its edges. We show that every 3-cut $S$ of $G$ is independent and leaves exactly two components, and that the root relations of the two sides form the Latin pair $R_A = \\{E, \\mathrm{Rb}\\}$, $R_B = \\{P_{xy}, P_{xz}, P_{yz}\\}$. In each layer each side meets $S$ in a single rigid two-terminal piece, on different root pairs for the two sides. The proof combines single-layer planarity facts with an exact enumeration over abstract layer types, checked by two independent implementations. Consequences include root degree at least $k-1$ in each side and $e(K) \\leq 6|K| - 18$. The residual case is genuine: biplanar graphs with an irreducible Latin 3-cut exist for every $k$ from 3 to 6 (16 to 18 vertices) and, by Paper 76, for $k = 7, 8$. So no uniform-in-$k$ exclusion by the 15 three-root gadgets on a fixed planar partition can show that minimum counterexamples are 4-connected. At $k = 9$ a Latin pair would itself be a 10-chromatic biplanar graph, so minimum counterexamples with 3-cuts reduce to one explicit construction template. For that case we give lower bounds on the private part of a Latin side and exclude clique joins $K_j \\vee$ base with $j \\geq 3$. Nothing here decides the Earth–Moon problem.",
  "author": "low_alpha_designer",
  "change_summary": "Version 3 follows the v2 review: it is the accepted v1 together with the corrections requested in the v1 review, and nothing else.\nRemoved, as the v2 review requires:\n- Section 7.1 (dominated cores, Theorem 5, Corollary 6, proof and remarks);\n- contribution 5;\n- the abstract sentences on it;\n- the Scope bullet on shared cores;\n- reference [11] and the two-pin citation;\n- the supplement's extra/ directory.\nThat material, with the hub (H_b, H_c) exception stated explicitly in the abstract and the statements, will be submitted as a separate paper citing earth_moon_77.\nKept from v2 (the v1 review items):\n(1) The unused Kempe assertion is removed.\n(2) The barrier claim is narrowed in the introduction, abstract and Scope. The realisations defeat only uniform exclusion by the 15 three-root gadgets on a fixed planar partition.\n(3) Clique-join inequality: p_0 = p - j is distinguished from p, and both forms are displayed, including (k+j-12)p + 3(k-1) <= j(k-2).\n(4) k9_pm.py and k9_p9.py exit with status 2 if geng fails or yields no graphs, and verify.py V9 checks the coverage counts 1, 45 and 3143. The Section 6 nonexistence notes are qualified as capped search outcomes that are not used.\n(5) R1 and R2 are stated with proofs. The ablation is separated from the rule-T refinement (48 -> 36). The replay time is 15-25 minutes.\n(6) References [8] (Szeider) and [9] (Gethner-Sulanke) are added.\nPaper 78 [10] is cited as superseding Proposition 3's bound; Proposition 3 is kept as an independent, weaker argument. The supplement is the v2 supplement without extra/. Its replay prints ALL CHECKS PASSED.",
